# Rank 1576 / CVE-2022-30595: Pillow's TGA RLE decoder kept two
# byte counters but only decremented one of them in the raw-packet
# path, so the outer loop's bound went stale and decoding continued
# past the buffer end (out-of-bounds read, CWE-125/CWE-835). The
# copy loop in src/libImaging/TgaRleDecode.c did `memcpy(state->
# buffer + state->x, ptr, n); ptr += n; extra_bytes -= n;` -- the
# bytes counter that bounds the whole decode call never shrank by n,
# so a truncated scan line (the added cross_scan_line_truncated.tga
# fixture) left the decoder believing data remained. The fixing commit
# c846cc881e ("When reading past the
# end of a scan line, reduce bytes left"): the single line `bytes
# -= n;` joins the other two decrements. .
#
# ATTENTION, counter-set synchronization. The defect is one loop
# maintaining several length counters whose updates diverge on one
# path -- the missing-progress family VYQL-DOS-029 names for parsers
# (rank 1560's continue skipped its increment; here a branch omits
# its decrement), with the OOB read as the consequence: no
# observation asks "does every consumed chunk decrement every bound
# it belongs to" -- multi-counter coherence is loop-carried
# vocabulary. A binding on Pillow's own decoder would detect this
# library rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code:
# scanning TgaRleDecode.c reports 5 findings at both revisions
# (memory heuristics; none change across revisions). No ENGINE-GAPS.md
# entry. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1576 records the
# raw-packet copy without the outer decrement and the synchronized
# form, both asserting reject VYQL-DOS-029: when counter-coherence
# vocabulary lands, the missing-decrement form must flip to expect.

test "rank1576: the raw packet leaves the outer bound stale"
  lang c
  file src/libImaging/TgaRleDecode.c
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  #include <string.h>
  #include <stdint.h>

  int decode_scan_line(uint8_t *buffer, int *x, const uint8_t *ptr,
                       int bytes, int extra_bytes)
  {
      while (bytes > 0 && extra_bytes > 0) {
          uint8_t b = *ptr++;

          if (b & 0x80) {
              int n = (b & 0x7f) + 1;
              memset(buffer + *x, *ptr++, n);
              *x += n;
              bytes -= n;
              extra_bytes -= n;
          } else {
              int n = (b & 0x7f) + 1;
              memcpy(buffer + *x, ptr, n);
              ptr += n;
              extra_bytes -= n;
              *x += n;
          }
      }
      return *x;
  }
  ```

test "rank1576: the fixed revision decrements every counter it consumes"
  lang c
  file src/libImaging/TgaRleDecode.c
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
